+    <main class="chapter-main" id="main-content">
+      <header class="hero hero--fleet">
+        <span class="hero__chapter">Agentic Horizon · Lesson 12 · Tactic: Orchestrate Your Agents</span>
+        <h1>Multi-Agent Orchestration: The O-Agent</h1>
+        <p class="hero__dek">When the interface becomes the wall, put one thin custom agent in front of the fleet. Give it lifecycle tools, protect its context, and review every result through observability.</p>
+        <ul class="hero__meta" aria-label="Chapter details">
+          <li>Video spine · 56:08</li>
+          <li>Core lab · 120–180 min</li>
+          <li>Course repo · multi-agent-orchestration</li>
+          <li>11 verified 1920×1080 frames</li>
+        </ul>
+        <p class="hero__promise"><strong>Mastery promise.</strong> By the end, you will be able to explain why orchestration follows custom agents, read the O-agent through its core four, map all eight management tools to CRUD, distinguish primary agents from sub-agents, trace the observability pipeline, run the prompt-driven sleep-check loop, and conduct a plan → build → review fleet without becoming its hidden workflow engine.</p>
+
+        <div class="scale-ladder" role="img" aria-label="Agent scale ladder from base through orchestrated agents">
+          <div class="scale-ladder__step"><b>Base</b><span>Use the capable general agent.</span></div>
+          <div class="scale-ladder__step"><b>Better</b><span>Improve its context and instructions.</span></div>
+          <div class="scale-ladder__step"><b>More</b><span>Add compute through additional agents.</span></div>
+          <div class="scale-ladder__step"><b>Custom</b><span>Control the core four for a domain.</span></div>
+          <div class="scale-ladder__step scale-ladder__step--destination"><b>Orchestrated</b><span>Command the fleet through one interface.</span></div>
+        </div>
+      </header>
+
