354:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><strong>Checkpoint 0 · 10/10</strong><p>Migration output applies nine migrations and exposes six tables: <code>orchestrator_agents</code>, <code>agents</code>, <code>prompts</code>, <code>agent_logs</code>, <code>system_logs</code>, <code>orchestrator_chat</code>. Health JSON reports healthy, the UI opens on 5175, and the connection indicator is green.</p></div>
358:          <div class="lab-box__meta"><span>Part 1 · Source trace</span><span>15 points · 20 min · required</span></div>
369:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><strong>Checkpoint 1 · 15/15</strong><p>Your worksheet points to exact source files, names all eight tools and parameters, and explains why the O-agent’s fully overwritten prompt makes it a custom meta-agent rather than a general coding agent.</p></div>
373:          <div class="lab-box__meta"><span>Part 2 · Fan-out</span><span>15 points · 20–30 min · required</span></div>
386:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><strong>Checkpoint 2 · 15/15</strong><p>One human prompt produces at least three create and three command actions, three independently observable sessions, and the exact audit artifact. Deduct 3 if the artifact lacks traceable course paths; fail the checkpoint if you manually launched a worker.</p></div>
390:          <div class="lab-box__meta"><span>Part 3 · Observe + lifecycle</span><span>15 points · 20 min · required</span></div>
394:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><strong>Checkpoint 3 · 15/15</strong><p>Evidence includes all four event filters, one regex result, one diff, one same-session follow-up, list/status tool actions, three delete actions, an empty active rail, and a surviving artifact. Your explanation uses the phrase <strong>soft archive</strong>.</p></div>
398:          <div class="lab-box__meta"><span>Part 4 · Ecosystem interop</span><span>10 points · 15–20 min · required</span></div>
401:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><strong>Checkpoint 4 · 10/10</strong><p>Evidence shows a managed agent running both <code>/question</code> and <code>/prime</code>, the context loaded by prime, the template’s declared Haiku/Read-Glob-Grep surface, and a correct primary-versus-sub-agent explanation.</p></div>
405:          <div class="lab-box__meta"><span>Part 5 · Orchestration workflow</span><span>20 points · 30–45 min · required</span></div>
426:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><strong>Checkpoint 5 · 20/20</strong><p>All three roles are identified correctly; the three documentation artifacts exist; every referenced path is course-local; the reviewer issues a verdict; and you can point to the prompt lines that create the sleep-check loop.</p></div>
430:          <div class="lab-box__meta"><span>Part 6 · Judgment + teach-back</span><span>15 points · 15–20 min · required</span></div>
435:          <div class="lab-box__pass"><strong>Checkpoint 6 · 15/15</strong><p>You produced both three-item lists, mapped a real job through all four PITER stages with rejectable review evidence, and your explanation includes Reduce and Delegate, observability, session persistence, soft archive semantics, and a task-shape judgment.</p></div>
453:          <li><strong>10:</strong> six-table infrastructure healthy at 9403/5175.</li>
454:          <li><strong>15:</strong> O-agent core four and eight tools source-traced.</li>
455:          <li><strong>15:</strong> one prompt creates and commands three primary agents with a durable audit.</li>
456:          <li><strong>15:</strong> observability drill, same-session update, soft archive, and surviving artifact.</li>
457:          <li><strong>10:</strong> <code>/question</code>, <code>/prime</code>, template, and skill interop proved.</li>
458:          <li><strong>20:</strong> plan/build/review workflow with prompt-driven sleep-check and reviewer verdict.</li>
459:          <li><strong>15:</strong> three-vs-three judgment lists, PITER map, and accurate teach-back.</li>

